WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
A locator breaks
The shop renamed a button. The test still looks for the old one.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.000
Shield finds the same element
It finds the element the test meant, by what it is for, and clicks it.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.500
apply-heals writes it into your code
Each healed locator is changed where it is defined, ready for a pull request.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.500
A rerun with healing off proves it
When the next CI run passes with the new locator, the heal is Fixed.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.000
Now on the real screens
Northstar Shop, a demo project with a week of CI runs.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.810
Shield shows the heals of every run.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:24.750
Each test with a broken locator, and how often it healed.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.540
Before and after: the locator that broke, and the one Shield used.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.190
In the code: the change is proposed in pull request #58.

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:35.440
A rerun with healing off passed: the heal is Verified.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:41.790
The same heal is in the run, in RunSights.
